  "title": "Lancashire custard tart",
  "subtitle": "baked egg custard in a crisp sweet pastry shell with freshly grated nutmeg",
  "excerpt": "The Lancashire custard tart is a very plain, very good baked custard in a sweet shortcrust shell: nothing more than eggs, cream, milk, and a little sugar, topped with freshly grated nutmeg before the oven. It is the kind of straightforward baking that rewards attention to technique over complicated ingredients. The custard should be just set when the tart comes out of the oven, creamy and trembling in the centre, and it will finish setting as it cools.",
