  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lancashire custard tart is a very restrained recipe: the satisfaction comes from getting the custard texture exactly right, not from complex ingredients. The oven must be low (150°C) for the custard and you must pull the tart before it looks fully set; a gentle wobble in the centre when the tin is nudged means it will set to the correct silky consistency as it cools. Leave it in the oven a minute too long and the custard will be rubbery."
          }
        ]
      },
