      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make and blind-bake the pastry case"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rub {{unsalted-butter}} into {{plain-flour}}, {{icing-sugar}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} until fine. Add 2 {{egg-yolks}} and press together to form a dough, adding a few drops of cold water if needed. Wrap and refrigerate for 30 minutes. Roll on a lightly floured surface and line a 22 cm loose-bottomed tart tin. Prick the base, line with baking paper, fill with baking beans, and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "blind-baking",
                  "label": "blind-bake"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blind-bake"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at 190°C (conventional) for 18 minutes. Remove the beans and paper and bake for a further 8 minutes until pale golden and dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the custard"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Reduce the oven to 150°C (conventional). Warm {{whole-milk}} and {{double-cream}} in a saucepan over a medium heat until just below a simmer; do not boil. Whisk 5 {{egg-yolks}}, 1 {{eggs}}, {{caster-sugar}}, and {{vanilla-extract}} together in a bowl. Pour the warm cream mixture over the egg mixture in a slow stream, whisking constantly. Strain through a fine sieve into a jug."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fill and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Place the blind-baked tart shell in the oven on a shelf pulled half out. Pour the custard in carefully to within 5 mm of the pastry rim. Grate {{nutmeg}} over the surface. Slide the shelf gently back into the oven. Bake for 30 to 35 minutes until the custard has just set at the edges but still has a definite wobble in the centre when the tin is nudged. Remove from the oven and cool in the tin for at least 30 minutes before unmoulding."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
